@@ -323,6 +323,8 @@ Syzygy SHALL validate the verdict before it counts: its schema; that the packet
 
 The run record SHALL record the agent tool, version and model of the authoring, inventory and review contexts as the operator declares them; each context's session identifier as that session declares it in its draft, inventory or verdict; and for each inventory and review context its launch form, which is a new terminal or the shell-escape prefix, as the operator declares it; each is labelled Inferred and attributed to whoever declared it. Syzygy SHALL refuse an inventory or verdict whose declared launch form is neither, and neither SHALL count until its launch form is declared. Syzygy SHALL refuse an inventory whose declared session identifier equals that of the authoring session, and a verdict whose declared session identifier equals that of the authoring session or of the inventory session it reviews. The record SHALL distinguish what Syzygy observed, which is the packet Syzygy built and rebuilt from the frozen subject, its digest, and that the verdict names that digest, from what remains Inferred, which is that the review context read the packet Syzygy emitted, unaltered, that each session was a top-level session the operator started, in the launch form declared, and not a subagent or process of the authoring session, that each context was fresh, that the review context saw nothing beyond its packet, that the inventory context did not see the draft, that each verdict and the inventory were written by the session declared for them, the session identifiers themselves, and the inventory's completeness over the clone and its preparation from the whole source population. The review page SHALL disclose that distinction.
 
+An inventory or review session MAY be started before its input exists (owner direction `POLARIS-DOSSIER-WAITING-SESSIONS-2026-10-08`). At the start of a run Syzygy MAY write the inventory brief into the inventory session's directory, make a directory for each review session, and print for each session the command that starts it; the operator starts each such session as above, and neither Syzygy nor the authoring session starts, resumes or signals it. A waiting session SHALL obtain its input only through one Syzygy command named for its directory, which reads only the local file system and makes no network request; waits at most a bounded time, never past the run's declared deadline, and then tells the session to run it again; and before the session reads its input re-hashes it against the digest Syzygy recorded in the run's state directory when it wrote it, refusing on any mismatch. Syzygy SHALL deliver a review packet to a waiting session only by writing the packet and its digest into that session's directory as the next numbered round and recording the delivery, and only after the gates of REQ-polaris-generation-033, including the per-project provider statement for the waiting session's own declared agent tool, pass at that delivery; a delivery SHALL NOT change the session's declared agent tool, version or model. The command Syzygy prints for a waiting session SHALL pre-approve, where the agent tool offers rules that narrow, only read tools over the session's own directory (and, for the inventory session, the clone) and that one Syzygy command for that directory, and never a write or a general shell; where the agent tool offers no rules that narrow, Syzygy SHALL print no pre-approval and SHALL say so. A waiting session SHALL hand its inventory or verdict to that command, as content it passes to the command or as a file under its own directory that the command reads; Syzygy writes the content into the session's directory under the role's own file name (the inventory, or the verdict of a round Syzygy delivered), and only there, and checks it as REQ-polaris-generation-034 and this requirement check an inventory or a verdict. A waiting session SHALL NOT carry the execution permission of REQ-polaris-generation-033. One waiting review session MAY receive the packet of each later revision of its subject as its next round, and a verdict it writes on that packet is validated and counted under the rules above. For every counted verdict the review page SHALL disclose whether its session had received an earlier round, or declares the session identifier of an earlier verdict of its kind, and where it had, that the reviewer has seen its own earlier verdict, which may anchor this one. The delivery records, the delivered files and the declared session identifiers lie within the agent sessions' write reach: that a waiting session read the packet Syzygy delivered, unaltered, that the operator used the printed command, that the agent tool applied the printed pre-approval as written, and a reviewer's continuity or its absence are Inferred, and no surface states them as Observed.
